<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shefqet Vërlaci</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1877–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shefqet Vërlaci was an Albanian landowner from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbasan">Elbasan</a> and politician, a long-time rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">King Zog</a>, who had broken off an engagement to his daughter. After the Italian invasion of 1939 he became prime minister of the Albanian Kingdom under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-iii">Victor Emmanuel III</a>, holding office until 1941. Real power lay with the Italian lieutenant-general, and he died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shefqet-verlaci.jpg" alt="Shefqet Vërlaci" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luce Institute · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shefqet_V%C3%ABrlaci_(portret).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
